--TEST--
An array expression with nowhere to put its result is refused where it is written: a literal under `var`, `+` over two arrays, an element written through a temporary, `[]` in a read position, `list(...)`, and a destructuring leaf with no type — `rule:types/arrays`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/arrays-in-expressions
// Each line below is an array expression the language has no answer for,
// and each is refused where it is written rather than given a plausible
// one. They are asked together because the diagnostics are what a reader
// meets first, and one that stopped firing would otherwise leave a program
// running on a value nobody decided.
//
// `var` has no target type to check a literal against, and a literal whose
// elements have two types gives it no one element type to take
// (`rule:types/var-inference`).
//
// `$a + $b` is the PHP operation `Core\Arr::underlay` replaces, and the
// temporary write is the one `rule:types/arrays` cannot express: the array
// is separated before the element is written, and a temporary is not
// stored anywhere the separated copy could go back to.
//
// `[]` names no existing element, so every position but an assignment
// target is refused, and `list(...)` is gone in favour of the one
// destructuring bracket. The last line is that bracket without the type
// every leaf declares.
class Make {
    public static function row(): array<int> {
        return [1, 2];
    }
}

array<int> $a = [1, 2];
array<int> $b = ["k" => 3];

var $loose = [1, "2"];
echo Core\Arr::count($a + $b), "\n";
Make::row()["k"] = 1;
echo $a[], "\n";
list(int $x, int $y) = $a;
[int $p, $q] = $a;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0414]: `var` cannot infer an array whose elements have different types
%A
error[E0467]: `+` is not defined with an array operand
%A
error[E0700]: an array element cannot be written through a temporary
%A
error[E0481]: `[]` can only be assigned to
%A
error[E0230]: `list(...)` is not supported
%A
error[E0101]: expected a destructuring leaf's type
%A
error: aborting due to 6 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
